+# Task 3 Report: Incremental Source Refresh and Mapping State Machine
+
+## Status
+
+DONE_WITH_CONCERNS
+
+## Commit
+
+`a5d153bc` (`feat: refresh embodied mappings incrementally`)
+
+## Implemented
+
+- Added five whitelisted `SourceSpec` adapters and independent per-source incremental queries.
+- Each source receives its own cursor. A failed source records an error, rolls back its read transaction, and never emits a next cursor; successful sources remain usable.
+- Empty successful polls retain an existing cursor but do not invent a first cursor.
+- Kept the old repair CLI behavior and exposed the new adapter through `fetch_embodied_incremental_sources`.
+- Added conservative mapping transitions and an explicit allowed-transition table.
+- New mappings are persisted as `candidate`; their transition history is persisted as `pending_review`.
+- Existing mappings upgrade to `verified` only through Task 2 `can_auto_verify(events, as_of=effective_as_of)` with an explicit cutoff.
+- Unavailable-source batches emit no downgrade update.
+- Evidence resolving to incompatible nodes produces a `pending_review` conflict instead of choosing the first node.
+- Mapping writes and transition-history writes share one transaction; any persistence exception rolls both back.
+
+## TDD Evidence
+
+- Initial RED: focused command produced 8 expected failures because `embodied_refresh.sources` and `embodied_refresh.mappings` did not exist.
+- First GREEN attempt: 7 passed, 1 failed; the remaining assertion incorrectly looked for `pending_review` in the mapping row instead of the transition review row.
+- Corrected contract: mapping status is `candidate`, transition review status is `pending_review`.
+- Strengthened rollback test tracks pending/persisted mapping and history state and confirms both remain empty after failure.
+
+## Fresh Verification
+
+- `bash tools/codex-lowio.sh py tools/tests/test_embodied_refresh_sources.py tools/tests/test_embodied_refresh_mappings.py tools/tests/test_embodied_refresh_repository.py tools/tests/test_embodied_refresh_evidence.py -q`
+  - exit 0; 37 passed.
+- `python3 -m py_compile tools/embodied_refresh/*.py tools/repair_priority_supply_chains.py`
+  - exit 0.
+- Task-file `git diff --check` and staged `git diff --cached --check`
+  - exit 0.
+- Commit hook lint
+  - passed.
+
+## Concerns
+
+- Conflict records are returned as explicit `MappingConflict(review_status="pending_review")` objects for the orchestrator/review layer. The existing database history tables require a concrete `mapping_id`, so a conflict between two brand-new nodes is intentionally not forced into one of those rows; doing so would require either picking a node or adding a dedicated conflict-table migration outside Task 3 scope.
+- Source adapters use trusted static table/column specifications. Adding a source requires code plus focused tests; arbitrary runtime table names are intentionally unsupported.
+- Parent-owned `.superpowers/sdd/.gitignore`, `progress.md`, and `task-2-report.md` modifications were not staged or committed.
