+## Review Remediation (2026-07-17)
+
+### Status and commit
+
+- DONE
+- `a95f26da` (`fix: persist embodied mapping conflicts safely`)
+
+### Critical/Important fixes
+
+- Corrected `fina_mainbz` incremental cursor from nonexistent `update_time` to real `end_date`; a live `information_schema.columns` test verifies the configured column exists in local PostgreSQL.
+- Extended undeployed revision `036` with dedicated `embodied_mapping_conflicts` and `embodied_mapping_transitions` tables. Both carry nullable run/mapping links, chain/company/node identity, evidence IDs, source identity, review/status fields, and timestamps.
+- Conflict rows now persist inside the same transaction as mapping work. A failure rolls back mappings, transitions, and conflicts together.
+- Mapping lookup now locks every existing row for `(chain_id, code)` before comparing proposed nodes. A proposed node incompatible with an existing node creates a persisted review conflict and does not create/update a mapping.
+- Multiple evidence batches for one `(chain_id, code, node_id)` are merged and fingerprint-deduplicated before calling Task 2 `can_auto_verify(..., as_of=...)`. Transition evidence IDs reflect the merged set.
+- Mapping state changes no longer write to `business_tag_stage_transition_log`; they use the dedicated mapping-transition table.
+- Caller-owned database connections use per-source savepoints. A failed source rolls back only to its savepoint and cannot roll back unrelated caller work; other sources continue.
